msgid "BEAST_PLAGUE_RAT"
msgstr "Plague Frog"

msgid "BEAST_PLAGUE_RAT_LEGEND"
msgstr "In medieval Europe rats were tied to the Black Death: their fleas spread the plague that killed much of the population. Here they are the Spider Sorcerer's familiars, tainted by his pact with the demon — bigger, red-eyed, attacking in swarms."

msgid "BEAST_PLAGUE_RAT_HINT"
msgstr "A rat's a rat: it fears fire. Bring a torch... or a mage who knows how to light one."

msgid "BEAST_MUTANT_RAT"
msgstr "Mutant Frog"

msgid "BEAST_MUTANT_RAT_LEGEND"
msgstr "The same plague superstition; tales of rats as big as dogs in the cellars are common in port towns. These are the Queen's older young, grown to the size of a hunting dog."

msgid "BEAST_MUTANT_RAT_HINT"
msgstr "There's a rat down there the size of a dog. Burn it and it runs."

msgid "BEAST_PLAGUE_BAT"
msgstr "Plague Bat"

msgid "BEAST_PLAGUE_BAT_LEGEND"
msgstr "In European folklore bats are an ill omen, tied to witches and vampires. Here they sleep on the tunnel ceilings and drop on whoever passes."

msgid "BEAST_PLAGUE_BAT_HINT"
msgstr "Look up in the tunnels. If the ceiling moves, it's them. Stones at them and they drop."

msgid "BEAST_ACID_TOAD"
msgstr "Acid Toad"

msgid "BEAST_ACID_TOAD_LEGEND"
msgstr "In European folklore toads were tied to witchcraft and poison — and some real toads have toxic skin. Here swollen toads spit acid that eats the floor."

msgid "BEAST_ACID_TOAD_HINT"
msgstr "Their spit melts boots. They're creatures of foul water: one lightning bolt and they burst."

msgid "BEAST_SEWER_GATOR"
msgstr "Sewer Gator"

msgid "BEAST_SEWER_GATOR_LEGEND"
msgstr "The famous urban legend of alligators in the sewers: animals flushed down the pipes that grew in the dark. Here they are huge and pale, hidden in the channels."

msgid "BEAST_SEWER_GATOR_HINT"
msgstr "If the water bubbles, get away. It lives at the bottom of the channel. Lightning in the water and it comes up belly-up."

msgid "BEAST_DEMON_RAT_QUEEN"
msgstr "Spider Sorcerer"

msgid "BEAST_DEMON_RAT_QUEEN_LEGEND"
msgstr "In German folklore a 'rat king' is a knot of rats bound by their tails, an omen of plague. Here she was the mother of all the sewer's rats; when Tortuga poisoned and burned her young, she made a pact with a demon, grew as big as a cart and nests on the lost war treasure, wearing the fallen king's crown."

msgid "BEAST_DEMON_RAT_QUEEN_HINT"
msgstr "Just bring fire. She already knows what fire is — and she hates it."

