msgstr "Portal to the Royal Capital"

msgid "ARENA_FARM"
msgstr "Farm"

msgid "PROP_TO_FARM"
msgstr "Path to the Farm"

msgid "NPC_VILLAGE_HUNTER"
msgstr "Bertram the Hunter"

msgid "NPC_VILLAGE_WIFE"
msgstr "Elara the Tanner"

msgid "NPC_ELF_ARCHER"
msgstr "Aeliana the Ranger"

msgid "DLG_ARCHER_1"
msgstr "Hold. Walk softly — you are loud for people who mean to live. I am Aeliana; I have watched this wood since before Ferncroft had a name."

msgid "DLG_ARCHER_2"
msgstr "The Leshy sleeps at the far end of the grove, under the elder tree. Bark, stone and rage. Every arrow I loose just feeds the moss."

msgid "DLG_ARCHER_3"
msgstr "Put it down and the forest will breathe again. Fire is the one thing the old bark fears. Do this, and I'll make it worth your while."

msgid "DLG_ARCHER_ACTIVE"
msgstr "Follow the stone path to the end of the grove. The Leshy charges from afar — do not stand your ground. Burn it."

msgid "DLG_ARCHER_DONE"
msgstr "The grove is quiet. I felt the elder tree sigh. My thanks, travelers — the wood remembers its friends."

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_LESHY"
msgstr "The Elder of the Grove"

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_LESHY_DESC"
msgstr "Aeliana the Ranger asks you to slay the Leshy, the bark-and-stone giant that guards the elder tree. It is Earth — it fears Fire."

msgid "DLG_HUNTER_1"
msgstr "Strangers! Mind the hedge when you leave — the grove is not what it was. I'm Bertram. Elara and I are all that's left of Ferncroft."

msgid "DLG_HUNTER_2"
msgstr "Something crawls out of the dark in the grove: lean, green, all claws. Three of them took my last deer and the rest of my patience."

msgid "DLG_HUNTER_3"
msgstr "Clear them out and I'll pay what I can. They're Earth-blooded things — they hate Fire."

msgid "DLG_HUNTER_ACTIVE"
msgstr "Three of them, in the grove, past the stones. Fire, remember. Fire."

msgid "DLG_HUNTER_DONE"
msgstr "Quiet at last! The deer are coming back. If you want more, talk to the Hermit and the Keeper in the squares."

msgid "DLG_WIFE_1"
msgstr "Don't mind the smell, it's the hides. I'm Elara. Bertram says you fight what hunters cannot."

msgid "DLG_WIFE_2"
msgstr "Stones have started to walk in these woods, trampling where our paths used to be. My racks, my fish… everything. The ones who know how to wake and tame such things are the Hermit of the Stone and the Keeper of the Pyre, in the squares along the trail."

msgid "DLG_WIFE_3"
msgstr "Talk to them — and come back in one piece. The things inside the caves — toads, bats, reptiles and beasts — are no joke either."

msgid "DLG_WIFE_ACTIVE"
msgstr "Stone and fire sleep in the squares — talk to the Hermit and the Keeper. The ice one is to the east."

msgid "DLG_WIFE_DONE"
msgstr "The woods are breathing again. Ferncroft thanks you — take what we saved."

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_REPTILES"
msgstr "Lurkers in the Grove"

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_REPTILES_DESC"
msgstr "Bertram the Hunter asks you to clear the pack of Forest Reptiles from the grove. They are Earth — they fear Fire."

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_GOLEMS"
msgstr "Walking Stones"

msgid "QUEST_FOREST_GOLEMS_DESC"
msgstr "Elara the Tanner asks you to defeat the Stone, Ice and Fire Golems of the Forest: the stone and fire ones sleep in the squares and only wake when the Hermit and the Keeper call them."

msgid "PROP_VILLAGE_SIGN"
msgstr "Ferncroft"

msgid "PROP_VILLAGE_SIGN_TEXT"
msgstr "Ferncroft — half a dozen houses, one hunter and one tanner. Strangers welcome."

